      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is the right approach.\n\n1. If we switch from charging on port 0 to charging on port 1, discharge will never be enabled.\n\n2. Even in the case where a single port is connected, we won\u0027t enable our discharge until VBUS crosses some voltage threshold (eg. we won\u0027t enable discharge until we _already_ naturally discharge to some degree).\n\nIn this CL, we enable discharging in certain cases where we need to bring down VBUS quickly (on power role swap):\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/362761/\n\nIs this not sufficient for your device? Do we really need to enable discharge on simple unplug of a power source? Why?",
